# Moodle PChat Comparison

Version: 1.0
Status: Draft

---

# Purpose

This document analyzes existing functionality provided by the Moodle PChat project and identifies features that may be useful for the Speaking Portfolio System.

Reference Project:

https://github.com/justinhunt/moodle-mod_pchat

The purpose of this document is not to duplicate Moodle functionality exactly but to identify proven workflows and design patterns that may be adapted to SharePoint Online.

---

# About the Reference Project

PChat is a Moodle activity module designed to support formative assessment through spoken interaction.

Repository:

https://github.com/justinhunt/moodle-mod_pchat

According to the repository description:

> "PChat as a formative assessment tool for Moodle."

The repository also notes that it was developed for Sojo University.

---

# Why This Project Is Relevant

The Speaking Portfolio System has several goals that overlap with PChat:

- Student speaking submissions
- Audio recording workflows
- Speaking assessment
- Teacher review
- Participation analysis
- Learning analytics

PChat provides evidence that these workflows are useful in educational settings.

---

# High-Level Comparison

| Area | Moodle PChat | Speaking Portfolio System |
|--------|--------|--------|
| Platform | Moodle | SharePoint Online |
| Authentication | Moodle Accounts | Microsoft 365 |
| Audio Recording | Built into Moodle workflow | Upload from user device |
| Transcript Support | Existing implementation | AI-generated transcript |
| Transcript Editing | Limited/Unknown | Core system feature |
